WEBVTT

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.450
Doushisha. Number 10. Bleeding injury.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.120
Oh, no!

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.700
"You Can Do It! JAPAN Rugby!!!"

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.410
Natsusa?

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:42.700
Natsusa!

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.500
Get a hold of yourself.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.750
Oh...

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:49.830
The wound doesn't seem to be very deep!

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:52.580
If he stops bleeding in ten minutes,
he can go out on the field again!

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:55.410
Yuu. We should apply some
Vaseline and tape him up.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.450
Yes!

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.250
Natsusa-<i>san</i>?

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.450
Sorry. My hand slipped...

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:11.500
Let's apply pressure with a towel
a bit longer to stop the bleeding.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:12.870
Yes!

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.250
What is it?

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.410
Are you scared?

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:23.040
You're the one that's scared.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.500
Huh?

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.000
It's fine.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.790
There's a lot of blood, but I didn't
get a concussion. Don't worry.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:33.370
I wouldn't get worried after all this time.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:35.120
Really?

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.290
You're shaking. You <i>tsundere</i>.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:41.200
I-I'm not shaking!

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.080
Natsusa, didn't you cry when I got hurt, too?

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.580
--I didn't cry!
--Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:49.120
--Huh? Really?
--Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.830
You're pulling the skin on my wound!

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:52.910
It's your fault for saying unnecessary things!

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:54.540
That doesn't mean you should
aggravate the wound!

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:55.540
A little spit would be enough
to take care of something like this!

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:56.200
"20 Makoto Someya"
A little spit would be enough
to take care of something like this!

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.620
"20 Makoto Someya"
Spit?! Is your spit some kind of panacea?!

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.910
I'm telling you that hurts!

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:02.120
Shit!

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:06.330
It's only been a few weeks,
but I feel so nervous!

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:07.870
Makoto.

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:12.370
You probably already know,
but be careful of their number 8.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:14.330
I'll give you my complete support.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.540
Yeah.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.910
I'll protect Mako-<i>san</i>.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:28.370
Hey!

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:32.790
Here he comes!

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.080
Failure to release the ball.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:03.700
I wanted to copy that play style of yours.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.200
As expected of Natsu-<i>san</i>'s senior.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.830
What a terrible personality...

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.870
Like I thought, he's a really tough opponent.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.620
They got a penalty on us at a bad time...

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.160
Makoto.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.910
Be careful. Keep passing to the backs,
and we'll manage somehow.

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:30.080
Got it...

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:42.120
The moment Mako-<i>san </i>entered the field,
he went back to his old position...

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:54.500
Uchinashi. Uchinashi!

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.160
Join. Hurry.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.410
I see.

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:07.830
Ueoka is a threat, but I'm not...

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.660
Thank goodness.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:12.910
Nervousness?

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.450
How stupid.

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:17.950
No point in feeling nervous after
being looked down on so blatantly.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:19.910
Thanks to him, I remember now.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.290
Crouch!

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:22.290
Bind!

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:23.410
Set!

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:27.870
Push 'em down!

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.000
That's not enough!

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.250
We did it!

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:47.120
I had forgotten.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.040
For a long time now...

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:53.870
We'll kill you if you look down on us.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.500
Ikuto!

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:02.250
Shit! What should I do?!

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:03.750
This is it!

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.830
The best part of rugby!

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:16.040
Huh? Isn't this a bit tough?

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.080
That's not enough!

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.290
Way too tough!

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.620
I had forgotten.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:35.910
The expectations of my high school
and the pressure from my juniors...

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:40.370
I was caught up with all of that
and let myself falter.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:43.040
This fighting spirit that
makes you lose your mind...

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.080
Try!

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:50.000
...and the rush that wraps
around you when you score a try...

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:55.750
I had forgotten it all for so long.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.120
That felt so good!

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.580
All right!

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:02.450
Thank goodness.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:10.290
Gakuto!

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:12.500
Great job on the turnover--

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:24.540
Ever since I was young,
I was always the leader.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.000
"Currently Crossing"
Ever since I was young,
I was always the leader.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.540
"Currently Crossing"
Squad Leader Yufu!

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:31.660
Student President Yufu!

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.700
Captain Ikuto!

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.660
I always believed I was
supposed to stand on top

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:42.330
and that the comrades I made
were the best and most capable.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:43.370
"Youyama Saemon Hot Springs"

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:46.290
"Youyama Saemon Hot Springs"
"Three Years Ago"

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:49.080
What kind of attitude is that?

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:51.080
Are you trying to be captain or something?

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:52.290
What do you mean?

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.620
That haughty attitude of yours!

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:56.750
That doesn't make sense.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:57.750
What?

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:02.200
A person with a haughty attitude
wouldn't be fit to be captain.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:07.160
With those words, in a single moment,

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:10.750
I realized I was never a true leader,

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:15.580
and I became unsure
of what true camaraderie was.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.120
I see.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:22.200
The reason I played rugby
was so that I could lose against you.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.330
Ikuto, what's wrong?

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:28.950
I was meant to lose against you,
dedicate myself to you, and grow...

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:32.910
...so that I could learn
what true comrades are like.

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.790
--Blue wrapping paper, red wrapping
paper, yellow wrapping paper.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:46.200
--Huh? What?!
--Blue wrapping paper, red wrapping
paper, yellow wrapping paper.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.040
--Huh? What?!
--Raw wheat, raw rice, raw egg!

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:48.870
--I already interjected about that, myself.
--Raw wheat, raw rice, raw egg!

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:50.950
--I already interjected about that, myself.
--Raw wheat, raw rice, raw...

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.790
So stable.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:06.910
--Okay. Looks like it's time.
--Inhale... Exhale...

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:08.290
I'm off.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:13.040
Be good and wait for me.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:16.160
Why is he still so flippant at a time like this?

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:19.910
Did he go to a school that specialized
in making shallow men?

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:23.200
Did you go to a school that specialized
in the poisonous tongue, Natsusa?

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:28.790
"20 Makoto Someya"

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:30.250
"10 Ibuki Ueoka"

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.700
I'm leaving the rest to you.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.080
Mako-<i>san</i>.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.830
Take care of Taisei.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.120
Yes.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:53.950
Mako-<i>san</i>.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.910
"10 Ibuki Ueoka"

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:17.620
Kazutaka.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.750
Keep joining the scrum like this.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.620
We're changing our tactics.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:23.910
Now, now.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.290
Don't make such an unsatisfied face.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:29.160
The forwards on their side
are gaining a lot of momentum.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:32.620
Also, it looks like their number 9
isn't just there for passes,

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:34.200
so we need to be careful.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.250
Got it.

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:39.250
Okay! I'm depending on you!

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:44.410
You are so cool, Yasunari-<i>kun</i>!

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:50.120
Yasunari-<i>kun</i>?! What's wrong?

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:51.790
I want to see some videos.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:54.700
Oh! Yes! Of course!

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:57.200
I apologize that it's so messy!

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:58.500
What were you doing?

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:01.370
Oh, I was watching everyone's matches...

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.620
It gets this messy just by
watching some matches?

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:05.750
Oh...

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:08.450
Were you doing some analyzing?

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:14.080
I-I was just trying to imitate it!
I watched the analyst do it before...

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:18.870
B-But, I have the most data about
everyone from Maisagi High School,

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:22.700
so I thought I could do some analyzing myself...

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:24.910
I'm sorry. I did something unnecessary...

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:26.830
--Me...
--Huh?

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:28.250
Have any of me?

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:30.450
I-I do.

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:31.290
Show me.

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:33.200
B-But...

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.870
Just show me.

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:42.290
This isn't all of it! And my analysis
may be wrong in the first place!

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.580
No, it's right.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:47.000
It hurts because it's right.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:50.290
B-But you are so cool, Yasunari-<i>kun</i>!

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.750
Huh?

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.450
Your plays are so cool, Yasunari-<i>kun</i>!

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:56.790
Natsusa-<i>san</i>'s plays look pretty.

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:59.330
Seiichirou-<i>san</i>'s look uniform.

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:01.200
Ibuki-<i>san</i>'s plays are always genius.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:04.160
Saitou-<i>kun</i>'s plays look heavy.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:07.750
And Yasunari-<i>kun</i>'s looks cool!

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:11.620
That is something that can't
be shown through analysis!

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:18.290
I'm sorry. I guess I don't make sense.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.120
I don't get it, but...

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:22.660
Well...

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.830
Well?

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:26.540
No, it's nothing.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:29.410
Huh? What is it? Now it's bothering me!

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:31.000
I said it's nothing!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.580
But I might have made you feel bad!

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:34.540
You didn't!

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.160
--But--!
--It's fine!

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:38.200
More importantly! Madoka Hongou!

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:39.040
Huh?

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:43.040
D-Did you analyze Madoka Hongou-<i>san</i>?

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:44.750
He's also from Maisagi High School...

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:50.580
Oh, yes. I didn't analyze his plays
during high school as much, but...

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:53.410
I have done some analysis
on him in his college years.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:55.370
Since he's on an enemy team...

00:11:55.370 --> 00:12:00.750
When the backs charge forward,
he always stands in front of the goal.

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:03.870
We won't be able to get a try
if we can't take care of him.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:08.200
Can you think up a strategy using the
information you got of Madoka-<i>san </i>and me?

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.620
L-Let me try!

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:18.120
Yasunari!

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:25.620
Madoka-<i>san </i>doesn't have any particular habits.

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:28.790
I don't know if he does it on purpose or not,

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:31.120
but he defends by matching
the movements of his opponents.

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:34.370
That's why he's so hard to get past.

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:37.370
But because of that, we have the initiative!

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:49.160
First, you usually hold the ball
with your left hand,

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:53.160
but please switch it to your right
when you want to pass Madoka-<i>san</i>.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:57.500
Huh?

00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:01.910
Then, you usually swerve from the right,

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:04.080
so swerve from the other direction.

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:10.120
You might lose some time doing the actions,

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:13.370
but you'll definitely be harder to read!

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:16.870
All right!

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:19.120
As I thought, he's so cool!

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.370
Good job!

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.620
You did it!

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:25.500
Looks like your analysis was spot on.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:28.410
N-No! Not at all!

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:34.830
If you had told us earlier, we might
have won the last two matches.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:35.950
Natsusa...

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:39.410
I'll have you work your butt off
when we get to nationals.

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:41.450
Y-Yes!

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:43.910
Yasunari-<i>kun</i>.

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:47.620
You've really grown.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:49.410
Thank you very much.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:52.500
I've gotten some good comrades.

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:58.410
Really... He's grown...

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:08.200
We've finally managed to turn the tables.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:13.160
All right! We need to stall for time and escape!

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.370
Don't give the other team the ball!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:17.790
It's nice to see such honesty!

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:21.910
You aren't an enemy to me.

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.330
What?!

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:33.830
Ethan!

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:39.870
I'll stop him!

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:49.450
Try!

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.540
At a time like this!

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:56.290
Ethan.

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:01.830
Don't involve the team
with your personal issues!

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:04.580
There's a limit to being selfish!

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:07.160
No. No one wants to hear that from you.

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:09.160
You quit the team without a word.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:10.120
Exactly.

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:12.200
You ruined it!

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:15.330
Right. And Ibuki is just scared!

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:16.870
No! I'm not scared at all!

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:20.790
You look scared to me. You're holding back.

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:23.330
You've been doing good.

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:28.790
Everyone knows you've been giving your all
to the team these last few months.

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:31.660
You don't owe anyone anything.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:33.450
Aren't we a team?

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:48.870
All right! Miss!

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:53.790
It went in?!

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:01.580
This is the last play.

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:05.040
If we falter on the attack here, it's over...

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:13.290
There's something I've wanted.

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:17.410
I want to give my all to someone
without the calculations.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:22.080
I want someone to give me their all
without any calculation.

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:28.290
Yasunari!

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:34.750
To give myself unconditionally.

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:38.410
It's probably something called love.

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:43.700
Something that people born into
a loving family had a birth...

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:47.950
I desperately wanted something like that.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:50.410
Then!

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:55.250
Natsusa and Sei-<i>chan</i>
will become your family!

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:59.000
I want to tell my past self.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.660
It's all right.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:05.080
You'll definitely get it.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:12.950
As long as you don't give up,
you'll get it in a way you never imagined.

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:14.580
So...

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:16.790
Don't give up!

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:34.620
Try!

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:36.290
All right!

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:43.870
No side.

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:56.000
We did it, Ibuki!

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:02.040
Hey.

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:05.790
Get up already.

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:07.000
Give me a hand.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:08.500
Don't be spoiled.

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:11.450
More importantly! Ibuki!
You're bleeding too much!

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:12.790
I think so, too.

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:14.620
If I don't stop it quickly...

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:23.290
Kazutaka!

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:27.000
You better treat me to some grilled mea--

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.580
--Ibuki!
--Ueoka!

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:30.950
Ibuki is really gonna die...

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:40.040
Don't cry from a single loss.

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:43.040
We just need to crush them at nationals.

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:47.040
That's right. Touma, don't cry.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:49.790
But, even so...

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:53.330
Losing really pumps the adrenaline!

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:54.950
Natsusa-<i>san</i>!

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:03.120
Why?

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:07.120
Ow! Ow! It's painful!

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:11.750
It hurts. It's painful. I can't breathe...

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.700
Don't do strenuous exercise.

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:16.000
Huh? Why?

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.910
Why would you say something like that?

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:19.870
I want to play rugby!

00:19:19.870 --> 00:19:23.700
Won't you be alone?

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:27.620
I will! Don't leave me behind!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:32.540
Why?!

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:35.040
That's my number.

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:37.250
I love rugby this much!

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:39.910
I poured all of my heart in rugby!

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:42.750
Why can't I play?!

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:49.870
Sorry for the wait.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:52.620
Natsusa?

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:59.410
Sorry for pretending like I couldn't see you
and leaving you alone for so long.

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:01.250
No...

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:03.330
Is everything all right now?

00:20:03.330 --> 00:20:05.540
Yeah. It's all right.

00:20:05.540 --> 00:20:07.160
You won't cry?

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:08.700
I might.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:11.000
Huh?

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:13.250
But I won't be hurt anymore.

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:15.410
Like everyone else...

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.040
I've gotten stronger.

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:21.250
You worked hard.

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:23.620
Thanks for waiting for me.

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:25.250
No, it's fine.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.790
Can I stay with you again, Natsusa?

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:28.660
Yeah.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:29.790
Really?!

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:33.080
Yeah, I want you to stay with me.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:34.500
Come back home.

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.000
Thank goodness!

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:55.580
Welcome home.

00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:02.580
...goodness. Thank goodness!

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:11.000
Natsusa will be our
rugby manager and trainer!

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:15.870
I will probably cause you trouble
in the beginning, but I will try my best!

00:22:32.620 --> 00:22:33.910
Sei.

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:37.790
Are you happy?

00:22:37.790 --> 00:22:40.500
Yeah. I am.

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:42.040
I see.

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:52.790
Hey!

00:22:54.370 --> 00:22:57.790
Did that satisfy you?

00:22:57.790 --> 00:23:06.370
Got it. Then, I'll have to give my life
to you and rugby until you're satisfied.

00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:14.910
This is still just the beginning,
for both you and me!

00:23:14.910 --> 00:23:16.580
You're right...

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:19.040
Natsusa-<i>san</i>! Ibuki-<i>san</i>!

00:23:20.910 --> 00:23:22.910
They're calling for us.

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:42.580
"Thank you for all your support!"

00:23:42.580 --> 00:23:44.000
"Thank you for all your support!"
Here we go!

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:46.950
"Thank you for all your support!"
"You can do it! JAPAN rugby!!!"
